    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Runbook RB-208",
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "**Redis Thundering Herd Mitigation & Staggered TTL Recovery** — retrieved as `RB-208` by hybrid pgvector cosine + full-text search, fused with Reciprocal Rank Fusion.\n\nThe drafted plan calls `warm_cache`, and it waits: nothing runs until an SRE clicks `[ Authorize Cache Warm-Up & Orphan Purge ]` in the War Room. Batch key warming with jittered TTLs is what stops the herd from re-forming on the next expiry boundary — a single shared TTL is how the stampede happened in the first place.\n\n*TripleTen Cloud Platform — Autonomous Incident Defense*"
      }
    }
